WEBVTT

00:00:01.209 --> 00:00:02.623
On a building project,

00:00:02.623 --> 00:00:07.568
separate teams model the structure,
the ducts, the pipes and the cable trays.

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:10.769
When their 3D models come together,
they collide.

00:00:11.085 --> 00:00:12.662
These are clashes.

00:00:12.816 --> 00:00:15.397
And the 2D drawings often disagree
with the model.

00:00:15.965 --> 00:00:18.644
Finding all of this takes engineers days.

00:00:19.157 --> 00:00:20.767
AI could help.

00:00:20.829 --> 00:00:22.446
But does AI truly see?

00:00:22.792 --> 00:00:24.250
It can be confidently wrong.

00:00:25.262 --> 00:00:26.965
Our answer is Iris.

00:00:27.321 --> 00:00:28.503
AI proposes.

00:00:28.814 --> 00:00:30.204
Geometry proves.

00:00:30.307 --> 00:00:31.765
The engineer decides.

00:00:32.415 --> 00:00:33.772
Let's open the sample building.

00:00:34.797 --> 00:00:40.923
Northbank has four models
from different teams, with 1,732 elements.

00:00:41.379 --> 00:00:46.328
Iris finds 464 clashes,
in about 11 seconds on the cloud.

00:00:47.335 --> 00:00:53.309
Clash #1: a 600×300 supply-air duct runs
through a transfer girder,

00:00:53.309 --> 00:00:55.307
one metre deep, on Level 02.

00:00:55.553 --> 00:00:57.985
They overlap by 300 mm.

00:00:58.995 --> 00:01:03.762
Gemini 3.8 Flash proposes fixes
that are real edits to the model.

00:01:04.176 --> 00:01:07.837
Then geometry re-checks every one:
the clash is gone,

00:01:08.066 --> 00:01:11.293
the clearance is met,
and nothing new is hit.

00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:15.698
Here, Gemini's saved replies replay,
and every check runs again.

00:01:16.721 --> 00:01:19.454
All 8 clashes got a verified fix.

00:01:19.933 --> 00:01:24.499
On the 3 girder clashes, the fixes match
the human designer's real revision,

00:01:24.499 --> 00:01:28.920
exactly: the duct up 400 mm
through the web opening,

00:01:29.306 --> 00:01:33.217
the cable tray 250,
the cold-water pipe 280.

00:01:34.224 --> 00:01:35.483
See it for yourself.

00:01:35.958 --> 00:01:37.566
Before shows the clash.

00:01:37.857 --> 00:01:39.337
After shows the fix.

00:01:39.718 --> 00:01:42.646
Both shows them together,
in the same 3D view.

00:01:43.656 --> 00:01:45.262
The engineer decides.

00:01:45.529 --> 00:01:49.240
Nothing is applied until you press Accept,
with your name on it.

00:01:50.249 --> 00:01:53.901
The report goes out as a PDF
and a BCF file,

00:01:54.298 --> 00:01:58.776
for Revit, Navisworks,
Solibri and BIMcollab.

00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:03.422
Iris also checks the 2D drawings
against the same model.

00:02:03.862 --> 00:02:07.810
Here is sheet M-201,
the Level 02 mechanical plan.

00:02:08.819 --> 00:02:12.027
Gemini reads every tag
and size on the sheet.

00:02:12.548 --> 00:02:15.452
Here, the saved reading is replayed,
at no cost.

00:02:16.474 --> 00:02:20.227
Then each item is checked
against the PDF's own text layer.

00:02:20.704 --> 00:02:24.002
119 of 123 are confirmed.

00:02:25.021 --> 00:02:28.142
Iris compares the drawings
with the model's own data.

00:02:28.643 --> 00:02:31.323
On the clean sheet,
nothing differs from the model.

00:02:32.333 --> 00:02:36.688
A sheet with four planted mistakes
gives exactly those four:

00:02:37.169 --> 00:02:40.259
a wrong duct size,
a tray missing from the model,

00:02:40.499 --> 00:02:44.433
a duct that is really a pipe,
and a branch left off the drawing.

00:02:45.449 --> 00:02:47.635
But does AI truly see?

00:02:48.098 --> 00:02:52.424
For Track 2, Visual Task Factory,
we built Iris VisionBench.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:56.524
Iris turns its geometry
into a factory of visual tasks.

00:02:56.882 --> 00:02:59.368
It generates
synthetic building-services scenes,

00:02:59.496 --> 00:03:03.521
renders pictures of them, and asks
engineering questions in eight categories,

00:03:03.769 --> 00:03:06.917
from spotting a clash
to judging if a fix is valid.

00:03:07.919 --> 00:03:11.703
Every answer comes only from geometry,
never from a model.

00:03:12.151 --> 00:03:15.126
And integrity checks guard
against leaks and cheating.

00:03:16.457 --> 00:03:20.735
We tested Gemini 3.8 Flash
on 95 picture questions.

00:03:21.348 --> 00:03:23.729
With the pictures, it scored 58%.

00:03:24.326 --> 00:03:26.640
With no picture, 36%.

00:03:26.881 --> 00:03:31.046
With the wrong picture,
just 14%, so it really does look.

00:03:31.675 --> 00:03:34.140
Given the measurements as text, 90%.

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:37.558
So it reasons well from numbers,

00:03:37.698 --> 00:03:40.366
but reading geometry
from pictures is hard.

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:44.795
It was best at choosing
which element to move: 100%.

00:03:44.881 --> 00:03:48.930
It was weakest at judging
if a fix is valid, 27%,

00:03:48.998 --> 00:03:51.418
and at picking openings, 29%.

00:03:52.093 --> 00:03:57.225
On average it was 96% sure,
but right only 58% of the time.

00:03:58.248 --> 00:04:02.826
That is exactly why Iris checks
every AI answer with geometry.

00:04:03.832 --> 00:04:05.163
AI proposes.

00:04:05.435 --> 00:04:06.596
Geometry proves.

00:04:06.975 --> 00:04:08.681
The engineer decides.

00:04:08.951 --> 00:04:14.318
Iris runs on Google Cloud, with Gemini
on Vertex AI, Cloud Run and Firebase.

00:04:14.943 --> 00:04:16.279
Built by Techjays.
